Brown bag lunch
The Guana Tolomato Matanzas National Estuarine Research Reserve (GTM Research Reserve) will host its May brown bag lunch lecture at noon May 6 at the GTM Research Reserve Environmental Education Center (EEC).
The speaker will be GTM graduate fellowship student Schuyler van Montfrans who will discuss his work on the interactive effects of consumers; (the purple marsh crab and the marsh periwinkle) and drought stress (climate effects) on the creation and expansion of die-off of the marsh cordgrass in southeastern salt marshes. Bring a brown bag for lunch.
Reservations are required. Call the reserve, 823-4500. There is no cost to attend.
Mosquitoes and you
GTM Research Reserve and Anastasia Mosquito Control biologists will explore the Northeast Florida mosquito from 9 a.m. to 1 p.m. April 30 at the reserve's Environmental Education Center (EEC).
The workshop includes live mosquito demonstrations and a walking field trip to the Guana Dam's mosquito monitoring station.
Admission is free. However, seating is limited and reservations are required.
To register, contact the GTM Research Reserve, 823-4500.
